{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/628117-a-merit-that-lets-pandorans-regain-pyros-without-taking-it-from-prometheans","id":628117,"title":"A Merit that lets Pandorans regain Pyros without taking it from Prometheans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-15T16:48:33-07:00","id":628117,"title":"A Merit that lets Pandorans regain Pyros without taking it from Prometheans?","content":"Should I write this? Sure, it probably clashes thematically a bit. But aren't Prometheans the second rarest monster type, losing only to the Mummies? This makes me think that Pandorans can either go a very long time without feeling hunger pangs, or that practically all of them are in Dormancy. Maybe that's a feature instead of a bug. Prometheans with high Azoth can awaken Pandorans from very far away, even if they are just within the same city at the highest ratings. And Pandorans are unbelievably fast, as Scurry, similar Transmutations and horror stories among Prometheans can attest. That helps Pandorans evade the sight of normal humans and thus Dormancy. I'd give Pandorans bonuses for resisting Dormancy inflicted by normal humans if the former have a lot of Pyros within them.<br /> <br /> I'd probably make this hypothetical Merit a &quot;quick fix&quot; solution, possibly requiring the Pandoran to spend 1 willpower point per feeding roll. But what else can hold Pyros? Qashmallim use Essence, which might not be close enough to feed Pandorans. Perhaps objects/fauna/flora that have been caught in the right Wastelands or Firestorms? Could individuals caught in the ravages of Disquiet end up creating Pyros-infused objects somehow? Demiurges are the humans who usually control Pyros, I know. Could the presence or Numina of a Qashmal infuse an object with Pyros? Could Prometheans store Pyros within an object or person to bait and control Pandorans?<br /> <br /> In any case, I believe Pandorans can only get Vitriol from Prometheans or other Pandorans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T17:42:06-07:00","id":628149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/628117-a-merit-that-lets-pandorans-regain-pyros-without-taking-it-from-prometheans#post628117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Qashmallim use Essence, which might not be close enough to feed Pandorans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Qashmallim use Pyros, the manifestation of one of the Lilithim can awaken every Pandoran in an area, and &quot;Control Pandoran&quot; is a specific Numen available to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:04:34-07:00","id":628264,"title":"","content":"Do pandorans get merits?<br /> <br /> Anyway, with second edition, I wouldn't be surprised if alchemists can keep pandorans fed as well as centimanni. <br /> <br /> And I must say I'm kind of missing the point here. If most pandorans are dormant, so what? In a promethean story they aren't relevant until a promethean comes around anyway. <br /> <br /> However, in a crossover game, you might want to play off of the suggestion in Bleeding Edge of altered pandorans who can feed off of such things as mana and vitae. <br /> <br /> Or confuse the players by having them meet a pyros eating Cryptid, a &quot;pandoran that doesn't play by the rules.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:06:10-07:00","id":628267,"title":"","content":"firstly I'd like to point out that the only Pandorans that matter are the ones players interact with. A Promethean game in its own way guarantees them being awake for you to interact with.<br /> all Pandorans are born of either Prometheans or Demiurges thus often their presence whither many or singular comes with a rather personal and specific story. The narrative of that story should give you all the details you need on a case by case basis. Secondly, Pryos is a &quot;substance&quot; in the world of darkness not merely a fuel trait and what that means is through trial, luck or guidance Pandorans might be able to harness it from other sources then Prometheans but then the question is why are they interacting with the players Promeatheans at all?<br /> if you have an answer for your specific story, great. do you need a merit no.<br /> If the players are not Promeatheans and you want to use Pandorans in the story either down play Dormancy, eliminate it ,completely, or highlight it as a feature.<br /> <br /> asking if you need a merit, is like asking permission. Mechanical Permission from the game; a game presumably you are writing.<br /> <br /> *ninja'd*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:15:56-07:00","id":628281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/628117-a-merit-that-lets-pandorans-regain-pyros-without-taking-it-from-prometheans?p=628264#post628264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do pandorans get merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 227 of the 1e corebook: &quot;Sublimati can also learn Merits, and sometimes even Promethean Transmutations.&quot; The Lady of Chains in particular has a fairly extensive collection of connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:44:32-07:00","id":628626,"title":"","content":"Depending on story/setting needs, couldn't you just make a one-off weird item/location (which the World of Darkness is supposed to have plenty of) that is a font of Pyros for the Pandorans to feed upon? If they still need to be a danger to Prometheans, you could make the Pyros from the source &quot;taste bad&quot;, so Prometheans still might get attacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T07:14:23-07:00","id":629886,"title":"","content":"I created a Pandoran transmutation which allowed them to regain pyros by eating human flesh (as Pyros is supposed to be found in minute quantity in almost every living thing). I think they had to deal about 3 points of lethal in order to regain a single point of pyros. As such, they were encouraged to eat Promethean flesh rather than mortal one, and I used this as a way to bring my players into a Pandoran hunt, since simply leaving the town would leave the Pandorans to keep feeding on mortals and killing people.<br /> <br /> As everyone else said: whatever is needed for your story will work.<br /> <br /> On another note, I've found that a Centimani is usually very good at keeping Pandorans fed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T21:37:53-07:00","id":630677,"title":"","content":"Since sublimati can learn transmutations, couldn't the sublimati recharge using the vulcanus- electroshock recharge transmutation or turn fire into pyros through Sublimate Phlogiston?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:01:46-07:00","id":630690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/628117-a-merit-that-lets-pandorans-regain-pyros-without-taking-it-from-prometheans?p=630677#post630677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since sublimati can learn transmutations, couldn't the sublimati recharge using the vulcanus- electroshock recharge transmutation or turn fire into pyros through Sublimate Phlogiston?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's by no means a sure thing, much less a universal thing, but there's almost certainly space for something like a souped-up version of the Napalmists or a particularly adroit Gremlin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:14:34-07:00","id":637375,"title":"","content":"I could see this as useful for a game that's not soley based on Prometheans. Like if you wanted to introduce some elements of <b>Promethean</b> to a chronicle populated by vampires or even mortals, sure. However, I dunno that it needs to be Merit as such. Make it a Dread Power or a trick that can be done in times of dire need at the cost of Willpower...<br /> <br /> Meh, know that I'm not much for making a lot of new rules to dictate how a 'monster' works for a game. If there were a need for a player's character to have something like this, I'd consider a Merit, but for an NPC monster (as Pandorans are in the game), making it so by fiat works just fine for me. By all means DO give it some limits and rules, but yeah, it doesn't need to be a full-on Merit.<br /> <br /> As ever, YMMV, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}